            "text": "Created attachment 3942\npatch v2: close the zip handle when unzip() errors while extracting or listing\n\nOSS-Fuzz has since found the listing-path twin of this leak (testcase 6127770850361344); the attached v2 patch covers both.\n\nziplist(), behind unzip(list = TRUE), opens the archive and closes it only on its normal return or by hand before its own error() calls. The entry count it passes to allocVector() comes straight from the central directory, and a corrupt zip64 record can carry one that allocVector() rejects (the fuzzer's archive claims 0xff000001 entries, which the (int) cast makes negative). That error unwinds past unzClose(), so each failed unzip(list = TRUE) costs a descriptor, on R 4.6.1 and R-devel alike:\n\nle <- function(x, n) writeBin(as.integer(x), raw(), size = n, endian = \"little\")\nentries <- as.raw(c(0x01, 0x00, 0x00, 0xff, 0, 0, 0, 0))\nrecord <- c(as.raw(c(0x50, 0x4b, 0x06, 0x06)), le(44, 8), le(45, 2), le(45, 2),\n            le(0, 4), le(0, 4), entries, entries, le(0, 8), le(0, 8))\nlocator <- c(as.raw(c(0x50, 0x4b, 0x06, 0x07)), le(0, 4), le(4, 8), le(1, 4))\nzipfile <- tempfile(fileext = \".zip\")\nwriteBin(c(le(0, 4), record, locator), zipfile) # pad: minizip treats offset 0 as \"not found\"\n\nnfd <- function() length(list.files(\"/dev/fd\"))\nnfd()\nfor (i in 1:50)\n    try(unzip(zipfile, list = TRUE, unzip = \"internal\"), silent = TRUE)\nnfd()\n\nUnpatched, the second count is 50 higher than the first; patched, they are equal.\n\nThe v2 patch (against r90746, superseding attachment 3931) registers the close in the same CTXT_CCODE context in ziplist() and drops the now redundant manual unzClose() calls; the zipunzip() and unz_open() parts are unchanged. Also at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/387.",
